WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local Crisis Centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. It was around 6.30pm on Saturday, October 24, 1953, when 15-year-old Evelyn Hartley left her home in the city of La Crosse, Wisconsin. Mature and trustworthy, Evelyn had been tasked with babysitting the 20-month-old daughter of one of her father's colleagues.
我们的剧集涉及严肃且往往令人痛苦的事件。如果您在任何时候感到需要支持，请联系您当地的危机中心。如需获取保密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您应用程序或我们网站上本集的节目说明。1953年10月24日星期六下午6点30分左右，15岁的伊芙琳·哈特利（Evelyn Hartley）离开了她位于威斯康星州拉克罗斯市的家。伊芙琳成熟可靠，受托照顾她父亲一位同事20个月大的女儿。

2
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Evelyn had only been gone for half an hour when her mother, Ethel, was overcome by an urge to call Evelyn right away. She didn't know why, but she felt a need to check in with her daughter. Ethel expressed her concerns to her husband, Richard. He didn't share her worry. Prior to leaving, Evelyn said she would call her parents to touch base at 8.30pm. Richard had no doubt that their daughter, whom they called Evee, would ring in just over an hour's time as planned.
伊芙琳离开才半小时，她的母亲埃塞尔（Ethel）就产生了一种强烈的冲动，想立刻给伊芙琳打电话。她不知道为什么，但她觉得有必要确认一下女儿的情况。埃塞尔向丈夫理查德（Richard）表达了她的担忧。他并不认同她的焦虑。离开前，伊芙琳说她会在晚上8点30分打电话给父母报平安。理查德毫不怀疑，他们称之为“伊薇”（Evee）的女儿会像计划的那样，在一个多小时后打来电话。

3
00:01:29.000 --> 00:02:03.000
But 8.30pm came and went without the promised phone call. Richard Hartley dialed the number for the Rasmussen family whom Evelyn was babysitting for. There was no answer. He tried again and again, but the phone continued to ring out. Wondering whether Evelyn might have gone to one of the Rasmussen's neighbors' homes for some reason, Richard started calling some of them. No one had seen his daughter.
但晚上8点30分过去了，约定的电话并没有打来。理查德·哈特利拨打了伊芙琳正在照看的拉斯穆森（Rasmussen）一家的电话。无人接听。他一次又一次地拨打，但电话始终无人接听。理查德心想伊芙琳是否因为某种原因去了拉斯穆森家邻居那里，于是开始给他们中的一些人打电话。没有人见过他的女儿。

4
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:38.000
By 9.15pm, Ethel Hartley was convinced something was terribly wrong. Richard drove straight to the Rasmussen's home, which was less than two miles away on Heschelow Drive. On their driveway, Richard could see lights on inside the residence. He could also hear music playing faintly on a radio. Feeling slightly reassured, Richard knocked on the front door. Evelyn didn't appear. He banged louder and rang the doorbell.
到了晚上9点15分，埃塞尔·哈特利确信出大事了。理查德直接开车前往位于赫舍洛大道（Heschelow Drive）上、距离不到两英里的拉斯穆森家。在他们的车道上，理查德可以看到住宅内亮着灯。他还能听到收音机里隐约传来的音乐声。理查德感到稍微安心了一些，便敲了敲前门。伊芙琳没有出现。他用力敲门并按了门铃。

5
00:02:38.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Still, nobody came. Grabbing the door handle to let himself in, Richard found it was locked. He then peered through the front windows into the home's main living area. It looked as though no one was home. Richard hurried around to the back of the house where there was a rear door. It too was locked. He shouted while pounding on the door, but his efforts were in vain. As Richard paced the perimeter of the house, he suddenly tripped on something.
依然没有人来。理查德抓住门把手想自己进去，却发现门锁着。他随后透过前窗向屋内的主起居区望去。看起来好像家里没人。理查德匆忙绕到房子后面，那里有一扇后门。门也锁着。他一边用力敲门一边大喊，但他的努力徒劳无功。当理查德在房子周围踱步时，他突然被什么东西绊了一下。

6
00:03:16.000 --> 00:04:10.000
A mesh screen had been removed from the basement window and was leaning against an exterior wall. The window was open and Richard was able to maneuver his body inside. As he lulled himself into the dark basement, his feet found a small stepladder below. He straightened up and turned on a light. Lying at the bottom of the stairs that led into the house above was a small black shoe with tassels. It belonged to Evelyn.
地下室窗户上的纱窗被拆了下来，靠在墙外。窗户开着，理查德设法钻了进去。当他把自己放进黑暗的地下室时，脚下碰到了一把小梯子。他站直身体，打开了灯。在通往楼上的楼梯底部，躺着一只带流苏的小黑鞋。那是伊芙琳的鞋。

