his daughter hadn't survived her ordeal. There was simply too much. It was a particularly tragic thought as Ethel and Richard Hartley had already lost their eldest son to Polio seven years earlier. Ethel was too distraught to leave her home until Monday when she was taken to the Rasmussen house and escorted through the crime scene. She remained calm as she looked at the living room and the basement. But when Ethel saw the blood outside, she broke down and lent on her husband for support.
女儿没能挺过这场磨难。血实在太多了。这是一个特别悲惨的想法，因为埃塞尔和理查德·哈特利七年前已经失去了他们的大儿子，死于小儿麻痹症。埃塞尔悲痛欲绝，直到周一才离开家，当时她被带到拉斯穆森家，并被护送穿过犯罪现场。她在查看客厅和地下室时保持冷静。但当埃塞尔看到外面的血迹时，她崩溃了，靠在丈夫身上寻求支撑。

21
00:13:25.000 --> 00:14:06.000
Oh, my Evelyn, she cried. We know she isn't alive now. People in La Crosse had been so absorbed by the football game the night prior that it wasn't until they gathered for Sunday church that news of Evelyn Hartley's abduction spread. Hundreds of locals soon descended on the Rasmussen property to offer assistance or gawk at investigators. Police had to cordon off two blocks around the house to prevent the scene from becoming contaminated.
“哦，我的伊芙琳，”她哭喊道。“我们现在知道她已经不在人世了。”拉克罗斯的人们前一天晚上完全沉浸在橄榄球比赛中，直到周日去教堂聚会时，伊芙琳·哈特利被绑架的消息才传开。数百名当地人很快涌向拉斯穆森的房产，提供帮助或围观调查人员。警方不得不封锁了房子周围的两个街区，以防止现场受到破坏。

22
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:38.000
Although night had already fallen by the time Evelyn was taken, the moon was bright and street lamps were lit. Like the Rasmussen's, many residents along Heschler Drive had yet to install curtains or blinds in their newly built homes. Thus, they could see directly outside. Across the street, a couple had sat listening to music in a room with a clear view of the Rasmussen's house. Another man had been painting his basement's interior.
虽然伊芙琳被带走时夜幕已经降临，但月亮很亮，路灯也亮着。和拉斯穆森一家一样，赫舍洛大道沿线的许多居民尚未在他们新建的家中安装窗帘或百叶窗。因此，他们可以直接看到外面。街对面，一对夫妇坐着听音乐，房间里可以清楚地看到拉斯穆森家。另一个人一直在粉刷他地下室的内部。

23
00:14:38.000 --> 00:15:14.000
These was one of the homes that was smeared with Evelyn's blood. Many other neighbors were home as well. One had even been doing some late night gardening. Despite this, no one had seen Evelyn or her assailant coming or going. However, Elven Sotterbach had been sitting on his front porch at around 7 that night when two or three sharp screams suddenly rang out. Elven couldn't tell where the screams had originated, but they sounded to him like children playing.
这是涂抹着伊芙琳血迹的房子之一。许多其他邻居也在家。甚至有一个人一直在进行深夜园艺。尽管如此，没有人看到伊芙琳或她的袭击者来去。然而，埃尔文·索特巴赫（Elven Sotterbach）那天晚上7点左右正坐在前廊上，突然传来了两三声尖锐的尖叫声。埃尔文说不出尖叫声来自哪里，但听起来像是孩子们在玩耍。

24
00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:54.000
The final cry cut off abruptly as though interrupted by something or someone. Elven thought a parent had intervened to discipline the unruly children. Elven's wife, who was in the kitchen, also heard the screams. She thought they sounded less playful than her husband did. After her, it sounded like whoever was screaming was sending a message of, stop, get away from me. That night, Ed Hoffa had been driving through the area to pick up his brother-in-law en route to the homecoming game.
最后的哭声戛然而止，仿佛被什么东西或什么人打断了。埃尔文以为是家长介入管教那些不听话的孩子。埃尔文的妻子当时在厨房里，也听到了尖叫声。她觉得听起来不像她丈夫说的那么像玩耍。对她来说，听起来像是尖叫的人在传达一种“停下，离我远点”的信息。那天晚上，埃德·霍法（Ed Hoffa）正开车穿过该地区，去接他的姐夫前往返校比赛。

25
00:15:54.000 --> 00:16:35.000
At 7.15pm, Ed pulled into Sunrise Drive, which ran parallel to Hesla Drive. His car's headlights illuminated several people walking along the footpath. It was two young men, with the young woman sandwiched between them. The girl was staggering as though she'd had a few drinks. Ed paid them little attention as he pulled over and headed inside his brother-in-law's house. Five minutes later, Ed was driving again with his brother-in-law riding his passenger. He headed north on Sunrise.
晚上7点15分，埃德驶入与赫舍洛大道平行的日出大道（Sunrise Drive）。他汽车的前灯照亮了人行道上行走的几个人。那是两个年轻人，中间夹着一个年轻女子。女孩摇摇晃晃，好像喝了几杯酒。埃德没怎么注意他们，就把车停在路边，走进了他姐夫的房子。五分钟后，埃德再次开车，姐夫坐在副驾驶座上。他沿着日出大道向北行驶。

26
00:16:35.000 --> 00:17:14.000
A dark green two-toned 1942 Buick suddenly careened past in the opposite direction. Its driver was speeding, but Ed still managed to catch a glimpse inside as the car whizzed by. He was certain the car's occupants were the three young people he'd passed on the street minutes earlier. One of the men was driving, the other sat in the back seat next to the woman. She was slumped forward, her head pressed against the back of the driver's seat. It looked as though she might have been unwell.
一辆深绿色双色调的1942年别克车突然从相反方向疾驰而过。司机开得很快，但埃德在车子呼啸而过时还是瞥了一眼车内。他确信车里的人就是他几分钟前在街上经过的那三个年轻人。其中一个男人在开车，另一个坐在女人旁边的后座上。她向前瘫倒，头靠在驾驶座的靠背上。看起来她可能身体不适。

27
00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:54.000
Ed had written off the incident at the time as young people having fun. On Monday, he was at work when he heard that a 15-year-old girl had been abducted from a house just around the corner. Ed then reported his recollections to the police. He hadn't been able to get a good look at the car's driver. He thought the man behind the wheel might have been a local college student, but when police followed up with the student, they found he had an airtight alibi. Pitches of a car matching the Buick's description were given to petrol stations in the area,
埃德当时把这件事归结为年轻人在玩乐。周一，他在上班时听说一名15岁女孩在拐角处的房子里被绑架了。埃德随后向警方报告了他的回忆。他没能看清车司机的长相。他认为开车的人可能是当地的一名大学生，但当警方跟进调查那名学生时，发现他有不在场证明。警方将符合别克车描述的汽车照片分发给该地区的加油站，

28
00:17:54.000 --> 00:18:34.000
with employees told to keep an eye out for similar vehicles. Police also set up an incentive for people to volunteer their vehicles for searching. Members of the public were encouraged to drive to local petrol stations and allow the station's employees to check the back seat and trunk of their cars. Once they had been given the all-clear, they would be given a sticker that read, my car is okay. The sticker would be displayed in the car's window, along with the date of the search. Any drivers who refused to comply with the search had their details noted by the petrol
并告诉员工留意类似的车辆。警方还设立了一种激励措施，鼓励人们自愿让他们的车辆接受搜查。公众被鼓励开车到当地加油站，让加油站员工检查他们汽车的后座和后备箱。一旦确认没有问题，他们就会得到一张写着“我的车没问题”的贴纸。贴纸会贴在车窗上，并标明搜查日期。任何拒绝配合搜查的司机，其详细信息都会被加油站员工记录下来并转交给警方。

