00:18:34.000 --> 00:19:19.000
station employees who passed them on to police. 40,000 stickers were printed, and the aim was to search every car in the county. Ted Hoffer's sighting indicated that Evelyn was taken by two men working together. The question still remained, was it an opportunistic or planned abduction? Nothing had been stolen from the Rasmussen house, but maybe the man had broken in only to be surprised by Evelyn. As she had been covering for the family's regular babysitter, some speculated that perhaps the other girl was the original target.
印制了4万张贴纸，目的是搜查县里的每一辆车。泰德·霍法（Ted Hoffer）的目击情况表明，伊芙琳是被两名合作的男子带走的。问题依然存在：这是一起机会主义绑架还是有预谋的绑架？拉斯穆森家什么也没丢，但也许那个人闯入只是为了寻找财物，却被伊芙琳撞见了。由于她是替家里常驻保姆代班，有人推测也许另一个女孩才是最初的目标。

30
00:19:19.000 --> 00:20:03.000
The media wondered whether Evelyn Hartley was as squeaky clean as everyone believed. What if she had a secret life and ran away with a boy? This notion was entirely dismissed by investigators and everyone who knew her. It was far more probable that a pair of prowlers had taken advantage of the quiet streets that night to look for potential victims. One woman reported that recently she had been ironing clothes in her basement only to look up to see an unknown man staring through a window at her. He laughed and said, I'm going to get you.
媒体想知道伊芙琳·哈特利是否像每个人认为的那样清白。如果她有秘密生活并和一个男孩私奔了呢？这个想法被调查人员和所有认识她的人完全否定了。更有可能的是，一对徘徊者利用那天晚上安静的街道寻找潜在的受害者。一名妇女报告说，最近她在地下室熨衣服时，抬头看到一个陌生男人正透过窗户盯着她。他笑着说：“我要抓住你。”

31
00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:44.000
Investigators tracked down a man who was known to spy through people's windows. They also interviewed a man who had been convicted of sexually abusing his 12-year-old daughter six years earlier. Neither of these lines of inquiry led anywhere, nor did interviews with 48 other men who were wanted for or associated with the various sex crimes. Richard Hartley and Avigo Rasmussen were also looked into, but more so out of procedure than anything else. Both men cooperated with authorities and were ruled out of the investigation.
调查人员追踪到了一个以透过别人窗户窥探而闻名的男人。他们还采访了一个六年前因性虐待自己12岁女儿而被定罪的男人。这些调查方向都没有任何结果，对其他48名因各种性犯罪而被通缉或与之有关的男子的采访也是如此。理查德·哈特利和维戈·拉斯穆森也受到了调查，但这更多是出于程序而非其他原因。两名男子都配合了当局，并被排除了嫌疑。

32
00:20:44.000 --> 00:21:23.000
The cross residents, businesses and organizations pulled together a reward for information that was the equivalent of almost $71,500 today. Upwards of 2,000 people joined the search for Evelyn. Bodies of water were dragged, farmers scoured their fields and hunters were on the lookout while in the woods. Recently dug graves at cemeteries were checked in case Evelyn's attacker had thought to use one as an easy way to dispose of her. Many of those searching for Evelyn were her peers from her school.
拉克罗斯的居民、企业和组织共同筹集了一笔悬赏金，相当于今天的近71,500美元。超过2,000人加入了寻找伊芙琳的行列。人们打捞了水体，农民搜寻了他们的田地，猎人在树林里时也保持警惕。墓地里新挖的坟墓也被检查了，以防伊芙琳的袭击者想利用其中一个作为处理她的简便方法。许多寻找伊芙琳的人都是她学校的同学。

33
00:21:23.000 --> 00:22:08.000
They were joined by the local Boy Scouts and other community groups. Amongst the crowd was Evelyn's 22-year-old brother, Thomas. He had rushed home from college upon learning of Evelyn's disappearance. Thomas and a friend covered three miles of La Crosse, removing manholes and then jumping down into the storm sewers to check for Evelyn. When it grew dark, Thomas became upset. He didn't want to stop looking for his little sister. Wednesday, October 28 marked four days since Evelyn Hartley went missing.
当地童子军和其他社区团体也加入了他们的行列。人群中还有伊芙琳22岁的哥哥托马斯（Thomas）。他在得知伊芙琳失踪后从大学赶回家。托马斯和一个朋友搜寻了拉克罗斯的三英里区域，移开井盖，然后跳进雨水下水道寻找伊芙琳。天黑时，托马斯很难过。他不想停止寻找他的小妹妹。10月28日星期三，距离伊芙琳·哈特利失踪已经四天了。

34
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:48.000
Highway 14, two miles south of La Crosse's city limits had been searched the previous day to no result. Yet, on Wednesday, a bra and a pair of women's underwear were recovered from the area. The garments were a popular brand and appeared to be Evelyn's size. Given they hadn't been spotted previously, it was believed that they'd been dumped within the past 24 hours. They appeared to have been thrown from a moving vehicle that was fleeing south. Both garments were stained with type A blood.
拉克罗斯市界以南两英里的14号公路前一天已被搜查，但没有结果。然而，在周三，该地区发现了一件胸罩和一条女式内裤。这些衣物是一个受欢迎的品牌，看起来是伊芙琳的尺码。鉴于之前没有发现它们，人们认为它们是在过去24小时内被丢弃的。它们似乎是从一辆向南逃窜的行驶车辆中扔出来的。两件衣物上都沾有A型血。

35
00:22:48.000 --> 00:23:33.000
As roughly 40% of the population had this blood type, police couldn't be certain it was Evelyn's. These later, on Friday, October 31, a third search of Highway 14 was undertaken. Close to where the bra and underwear had been found, a search party came across two size 11 good-rich brand sneakers. They too had seemingly been tossed one at a time from a vehicle travelling south. The pattern on the soles of the sneakers matched the muddy prints found in the Rasmussen home. They had a distinctive circular wear pattern as well, which suggested whoever owned them
由于大约40%的人口有这种血型，警方无法确定这一定是伊芙琳的。几天后，即10月31日星期五，对14号公路进行了第三次搜查。在发现胸罩和内裤的地方附近，搜查队发现了两只11码的古德里奇（Goodrich）品牌运动鞋。它们似乎也是从一辆向南行驶的车辆中一只一只扔出来的。运动鞋鞋底的图案与在拉斯穆森家发现的泥泞鞋印相符。它们还有一个独特的圆形磨损图案，这表明拥有它们的人

36
00:23:33.000 --> 00:24:13.000
worked with some kind of machinery. The shoes also had type A blood on them. It was determined that they had been worn by two different people, one whose feet was a size larger than the sneakers. This particular model of sneaker was called the Hood Mogul. They'd been available throughout Wisconsin, Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Illinois, but hadn't been sold in Wisconsin for about three years. An unusual marking on the back of the shoes was traced back to a Whizzer motorbike, meaning
从事某种机械工作。鞋子上也有A型血。经确定，它们是由两个人穿过的，其中一个人的脚比运动鞋大一码。这种特定的运动鞋型号被称为“胡德大亨”（Hood Mogul）。它们在威斯康星州、爱荷华州、密歇根州、明尼苏达州和伊利诺伊州都有销售，但在威斯康星州已经有大约三年没有销售了。鞋子背面一个不寻常的标记被追溯到一辆惠泽尔（Whizzer）摩托车，这意味着

37
00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:53.000
whoever owned the shoes also rode this make of motorcycle. Registration and sales records for Whizzer motorbikes were checked, but the line of inquiry went nowhere. Two and a half weeks later, rumours had reached detectives pertaining to a blood-stained jacket. It had been found about 300 feet from where the sneakers were discovered. Rumours had noticed the jacket lying on the highway's shoulder as they drove past each day. One had picked it up and thrown it in the back of his truck, then promptly forgot about
拥有这些鞋子的人也骑这种品牌的摩托车。警方检查了惠泽尔摩托车的登记和销售记录，但这条调查线索毫无进展。两周半后，侦探们收到了关于一件血迹斑斑的夹克的传闻。它是在距离发现运动鞋的地方约300英尺处被发现的。传闻说有人每天开车经过时都注意到这件夹克躺在公路路肩上。其中一人把它捡起来扔进了卡车的后部，然后很快就忘了它。

38
00:24:53.000 --> 00:25:33.000
it. The police identified the farmer and took possession of the jacket. It was denim and looked like the kind of jacket worn by people who worked outdoors. It had been cut along the bottom, then re-hemmed with a sewing machine using white thread. This had resulted in strange, shallow pockets and, like the shoes, it had spots of type A blood on it, on the front, back and the sleeves. Smears of blood in the Rasmussen home looked to be the result of a denim type fabric being rubbed against surfaces.
警方确认了那名农民并拿到了这件夹克。它是牛仔布做的，看起来像是户外工作者穿的那种夹克。它的底部被剪开，然后用缝纫机用白线重新缝边。这导致了奇怪的浅口袋，而且像鞋子一样，它的正面、背面和袖子上都有A型血点。拉斯穆森家里的血迹看起来像是牛仔布料摩擦表面造成的。

39
00:25:33.000 --> 00:26:19.000
It seemed unlikely that the person who owned the shoes had also owned the jacket. The size 11 shoes indicated a taller owner, whereas a size 36 jacket would belong to a smaller man. Once again, clues in the case seemed to point to two perpetrators. The jacket had faded spots under the armpits, possibly caused by a safety harness commonly worn by people who worked as steeplejacks. They climbed tall structures like chimneys and steeples to carry out repairs. Detectives learned that a local man had manufactured safety harnesses for two steeplejacks the
拥有鞋子的人似乎不太可能也拥有这件夹克。11码的鞋子表明主人个子较高，而36码的夹克则属于一个较小的人。案件中的线索再次似乎指向两名肇事者。夹克腋下有褪色的斑点，可能是由高空作业者（steeplejacks）通常穿的安全带造成的。他们攀爬烟囱和尖塔等高大结构进行维修。侦探们了解到，一名当地男子在前一年为两名高空作业者制造了安全带，

40
00:26:19.000 --> 00:27:03.000
previous year, but all he remembered about them was that they were young and possibly from the area. These had the bloodied jacket and shoes toured through 31 different towns within a 40-mile radius of La Crosse. They were displayed at local fairs and in public places in hopes someone would recognise them. As all their leads dried up, investigators sought to polygraph test every male student and school faculty member within the area. This would amount to a total of around 1,750 tests, making it the largest mass polygraph
但他对他们的记忆只有他们很年轻，可能来自该地区。警方带着血迹斑斑的夹克和鞋子巡回了拉克罗斯方圆40英里内的31个不同城镇。它们在当地集市和公共场所展出，希望有人能认出它们。随着所有线索中断，调查人员试图对该地区的所有男性学生和学校教职员工进行测谎测试。这将总共达到约1,750次测试，使其成为美国历史上最大规模的测谎

41
